WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.070
Look down on a city: roofs,
roads, concrete and glass.

2
00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:10.490
The US Environmental Protection Agency
says an ordinary roof can reach 37 degrees

3
00:00:10.540 --> 00:00:13.250
Celsius warmer than the air around it.

4
00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:17.310
It has a name for warmer
built-up areas: heat islands.

5
00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:19.530
But weather is more than heat.

6
00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:24.010
Can a city of concrete, glass and
roads really make its own weather?

7
00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:27.790
In this mission, you'll follow a
temperature profile across a city,

8
00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:30.270
from the rural edge to the centre.

9
00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:35.770
Then you'll unpick a famous
fog: London, December 1952.

10
00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:40.050
Your mission: find out whether a
city can really make its own weather.
